  "critique": {
    "axis": "memorability",
    "evidence": "The red-mutator/blue-defense split, neon duel palette, emphatic thesis headline, and fraud-phylogeny concept create a recognizable arena metaphor across all viewports. However, the dominant presentation remains a familiar dark analytics dashboard: line chart, status pills, bordered cards, and dense lists. The phylogeny—the most distinctive visual—is tiny on desktop and reduced to ordinary rows on tablet/mobile, so the signature idea weakens rather than becoming demo-defining.",
    "fix": "Make the mutation-versus-defense encounter the primary visual: enlarge and animate the phylogeny or attack paths, visibly show mutations branching, surviving, and being blocked across rounds, and integrate the ASR curve into that battlefield. Preserve a compact, legible version of this signature interaction on mobile instead of replacing it with stacked dashboard rows.",
